// An ungerminated seed, and a `Powder` on purpose: seeds fall.
//
// Previously a seed was `wood` (Plant kind), which never moves, so one
// placed in mid-air hung there and germinated into a tree growing out of
// nothing. Reported from live play as "seeds stay where placed and do not
// drop... hard to place on the soil surface and unrealistic".
//
// Being a Powder means it falls, rolls down slopes, piles in hollows and
// comes to rest on the surface -- all of it from the CA rules that already
// exist, with no seed-specific movement code anywhere. It also means seeds
// scattered over uneven ground collect where real seeds collect.
//
// `Germinate` converts the landed cell to `wood` (plant.rs's `germinate`),
// so this material only ever exists before germination.
(
    name: "seed",
    display: "Seed",
    kind: Powder,
    // Light: a seed sinks through water rather than floating, but only
    // just.
    density: 0.6,
    // Steep, so seeds sit where they land instead of running like sand to
    // the bottom of every slope. Real seeds are irregular and interlock.
    // **A seed is round, hard and small, so it does not stay where it
    // lands.** 55.0 was a guess and it is the single largest brake on
    // reseeding in the box: `roll_reach_at` is `1/tan(angle)`, so 55 gives a
    // reach of **0.70 cells** and `stability_reach_at` (repose + 8) gives
    // **0.51** -- a seed at rest can look less than one cell along the
    // surface, which means a seed that comes down on a leaf, a twig or on
    // the pile of its own siblings never moves again. Measured on
    // `reseed_probe founders=1 species=herb frames=60000`: **1,446 seeds
    // borne, 82 germinated (5.7%)**, and of the ~200 standing at any moment
    // **157 were resting on plant tissue and 42 on a seed pile**, with
    // `ready` at **0 in every single sample**. Nothing in the germination
    // gate can ever open on those: it requires `water_capacity > 0`
    // underneath, and neither tissue nor another seed has any.
    //
    // 22 degrees is a real granular repose for small hard round grains
    // (wheat and rape sit near 23-27; sand, already here at 40, is angular
    // and rougher) and buys reach 2.48 flowing / 1.73 at rest -- so a seed
    // on a one-cell perch rolls off it, and a seed pile spreads to a low
    // cone the next seed can slide down instead of a steep heap that holds
    // every sibling above the soil.
    friction_angle: 22.0,
    colors: [
        (126, 96, 52),
        (142, 110, 62),
        (110, 84, 44),
        (156, 122, 70),
    ],
    // Burns easily and briefly, like the dry husk it is.
    flammability: 0.5,
    burn_temperature: 500.0,
    burn_duration: 30,
    burns_into: "ash",
    heat_conductivity: 0.15,

    // Concentrated plant matter. Same value as leaf for now; a seed
    // being worth more than a leaf is a real distinction and wants a
    // measurement, not a guess.
    food_energy: 480.0,
    // In MPa like every other value of this field. The hard part of plant
    // matter is the coat and the rind, not the flesh; level with `snow`.
    penetration_resistance: 0.2,
    food_class: -1.0,
)
